cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pysacd, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: pysacd
abstract: >-
  pysacd reads SACD (Scarletbook) images, and PS3 SACD Ripper servers, straight
  from Python, and writes DSF, DFF (DSDIFF), WAV and FLAC in one pass with its
  multithreaded C engine. It also ships pysacd-extract, a clean-room, drop-in
  replacement for sacd_extract: the same options, the same file names, the
  same bytes.
authors:
  - name: "The pysacd authors"
version: 0.5.5
date-released: "2026-11-23"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dsd-toolbox/pysacd"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/pysacd/"
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
keywords:
  - SACD
  - Scarletbook
  - DSD
  - DST
  - DSF
  - DSDIFF
  - FLAC
  - audio
  - sacd_extract
  - Python
